,"source":"published national returns, not MHCLG's England collection"}},"dossier":{"summary":null,"compliance":null,"documents":[{"title":"NOTICE OF DECISIONS TAKEN AT PENSIONS COMPENSATION COMMITTEE ON 30TH JULY 2026.","url":"http://democracy.caerphilly.gov.uk/documents/s56173/notice-of-decisions-taken-at-pensions-compensation-committee.pdf","committee":"Pensions Compensation Committee Decision Notices","date":"30/07/2026","key":false},{"title":"Provisional Revenue Budget Outturn for 2025/26.","url":"http://democracy.caerphilly.gov.uk/documents/s55973/provisional-revenue-budget-outturn-for-2025-26.pdf","committee":"Cabinet","date":"22/07/2026","key":true},{"title":"Provisional Capital Outturn for 2025/26.","url":"http://democracy.caerphilly.gov.uk/documents/s55974/provisional-capital-outturn-for-2025-26.pdf","committee":"Cabinet","date":"22/07/2026","key":true},{"title":"Treasury Management and Capital Financing Prudential Indicators Outturn Report For 2025/26.","url":"http://democracy.caerphilly.gov.uk/documents/s55976/treasury-management-and-capital-financing-prudential-indicat.pdf","committee":"Cabinet","date":"22/07/2026","key":true},{"title":"Provisional Revenue Budget Outturn for 2025/26.","url":"http://democracy.caerphilly.gov.uk/documents/s55798/provisional-revenue-budget-outturn-for-2025-26.pdf","committee":"Joint Scrutiny Committee","date":"06/07/2026","key":true},{"title":"Provisional Capital Outturn for 2025/26.","url":"http://democracy.caerphilly.gov.uk/documents/s55799/provisional-capital-outturn-for-2025-26.pdf","committee":"Joint Scrutiny Committee","date":"06/07/2026","key":true},{"title":"Treasury Management and Capital Financing Prudential Indicators Outturn Report For 2025/26.","url":"http://democracy.caerphilly.gov.uk/documents/s55801/treasury-management-and-capital-financing-prudential-indicat.pdf","committee":"Joint Scrutiny Committee","date":"06/07/2026","key":true}],"read_documents":[],"calendar":{"upcoming":[{"date":"2026-09-21","committee":"Governance and Audit Committee","time":"2.00 pm","status":"Confirmed; Special","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.caerphilly.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-22","committee":"Corporate and Regeneration Scrutiny Committee","time":"5.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.caerphilly.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-23","committee":"Cabinet","time":"1.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.caerphilly.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-29","committee":"Council","time":"5.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.caerphilly.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-08","committee":"Rights of Way Cabinet Committee","time":"2.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.caerphilly.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-13","committee":"Education and Social Services Scrutiny Committee","time":"5.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.caerphilly.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-14","committee":"Cabinet","time":"1.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.caerphilly.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-20","committee":"Joint Scrutiny Committee","time":"5.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.caerphilly.gov.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-07-30","committee":"Pensions Compensation Committee","time":"10.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.caerphilly.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-07-30","committee":"Pensions Compensation Committee Decision Notices","time":"10.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.caerphilly.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-01","committee":"Joint Scrutiny Committee","time":"5.00 pm","status":"Confirmed; Finance","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.caerphilly.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-08","committee":"Education and Social Services Scrutiny Committee","time":"5.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.caerphilly.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-15","committee":"Housing and Environment Scrutiny Committee","time":"5.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.caerphilly.gov.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Commercial estate income recovery is at risk; \u00a3100k of \u00a3200k saving is Amber","lead":"Council borrowing and financial standing often depends on property income. An income plan that is 50% uncertain in Q1 signals asset performance or market conditions are worse than budgeted.","iso":"2026-09-01","paper_title":"Appendix 2","paper_url":"https://democracy.caerphilly.gov.uk/documents/s56257/56257.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Parking tariff restructuring has \u00a370k Red in Q1 against \u00a3174k full-year saving target","lead":"Parking revenue is highly visible and price resistance from users may be forcing rollback of planned increases. Revenue shortfalls of this type must be covered elsewhere.","iso":"2026-09-01","paper_title":"Appendix 2","paper_url":"https://democracy.caerphilly.gov.uk/documents/s56257/56257.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Bowls clubs cost-sharing scheme is already generating undelivered savings in Q1","lead":"This is an early warning that community asset cost-sharing is encountering resistance. If this \u00a3300k full-year saving does not materialize, it will need to be replaced or reserves drawn.","iso":"2026-09-01","paper_title":"Appendix 2","paper_url":"https://democracy.caerphilly.gov.uk/documents/s56257/56257.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-01","committee":"Joint Scrutiny Committee","paper_title":"Appendix 2","paper_url":"https://democracy.caerphilly.gov.uk/documents/s56257/56257.pdf","headline":"Commercial estate income recovery is at risk; \u00a3100k of \u00a3200k saving is Amber","detail":"One of the few income-based savings is 'Commercial Estate Income Recovery and Growth Plan' totalling \u00a3200,000. Half of this (\u00a3100,000) is already flagged Amber (at risk) in Q1, with only the other half Blue (on track). The recovery plan is uncertain.","category":"income","matters":"Council borrowing and financial standing often depends on property income. An income plan that is 50% uncertain in Q1 signals asset performance or market conditions are worse than budgeted.","figures":"Total \u00a3200,000. Blue \u00a3100,000. Amber \u00a3100,000","quote":"Commercial Estate Income Recovery and Growth Plan. 200,000 100,000 100,000","material":false},{"iso":"2026-09-01","committee":"Joint Scrutiny Committee","paper_title":"Appendix 2","paper_url":"https://democracy.caerphilly.gov.uk/documents/s56257/56257.pdf","headline":"Parking tariff restructuring has \u00a370k Red in Q1 against \u00a3174k full-year saving target","detail":"The council plans \u00a3174,000 full-year savings by removing 1-hour and 3-hour parking tariffs and rationalizing parking charges. In Q1 \u00a370,128 of the \u00a3129,000 planned saving is Red (not delivering). This signals major risk to a material income assumption.","category":"income","matters":"Parking revenue is highly visible and price resistance from users may be forcing rollback of planned increases. Revenue shortfalls of this type must be covered elsewhere.","figures":"Full-year saving \u00a3174,000. Q1 plan \u00a3129,000. Q1 Red \u00a370,128. Q1 Blue \u00a358,872","quote":"removal of 1-hour and 3-hour parking tariffs and rationalise the existing parking tariffs to simplify the offering to customers. This is a part year saving to allow for implementation time, full year saving is \u00a3174,000. This saving has been adjusted for the generic 5% increase in fees & charges","material":false},{"iso":"2026-09-01","committee":"Joint Scrutiny Committee","paper_title":"Appendix 2","paper_url":"https://democracy.caerphilly.gov.uk/documents/s56257/56257.pdf","headline":"Bowls clubs cost-sharing scheme is already generating undelivered savings in Q1","detail":"The council planned to save \u00a3300,000 in full year by making bowls clubs pay 25% of maintenance in 2025/26 and full cost in 2026/27. In Q1 2026/27, \u00a345,000 of the planned \u00a3181,500 quarterly saving is already marked Red (not delivering), suggesting implementation is failing to land.","category":"savings","matters":"This is an early warning that community asset cost-sharing is encountering resistance. If this \u00a3300k full-year saving does not materialize, it will need to be replaced or reserves drawn.","figures":"Full-year saving \u00a3300,000. Q1 plan \u00a3181,500. Q1 Red (not delivering) \u00a345,000","quote":"Bowls Clubs will be expected to take on 25% of the cost of bowling greens maintenance in 2025/26 and full cost in 2026/27. The full year saving once achieved in 2026/27 will be \u00a3300,000","material":false},{"iso":"2026-09-01","committee":"Joint Scrutiny Committee","paper_title":"Appendix 2","paper_url":"https://democracy.caerphilly.gov.uk/documents/s56257/56257.pdf","headline":"Building Cleaning cost recovery will increase charges to schools by 44% and they may switch providers","detail":"The council plans to move building cleaning to 'full cost recovery' by raising the hourly rate from \u00a314.95 to \u00a321.47. The document explicitly notes that schools may choose to move to an alternative provider. The 2026/27 part-year saving is \u00a3523,096 with full-year savings claimed as \u00a32,092,385. Currently \u00a3440,610 is Blue (on track) and \u00a382,486 Amber (at risk).","category":"income","matters":"Service exit by schools would eliminate this saving, forcing the council to absorb \u00a32m in unexpected costs. A 44% charge increase is large enough to trigger procurement reviews by school governing bodies.","figures":"Hourly rate increase from \u00a314.95 to \u00a321.47 (44% increase). Part-year saving \u00a3523,096. Full-year saving \u00a32,092,385. Current: Blue \u00a3440,610, Amber \u00a382,486","quote":"move to full cost recovery of Building Cleaning service by increasing hourly rate from \u00a314.95 to \u00a321.47 (44% increase). CCBC services and Schools will need to either re-prioritise existing budget to cover the cost increase or reduce service level to stay within existing budget. Schools may choose to move to an alternative provider","material":false},{"iso":"2026-09-01","committee":"Joint Scrutiny Committee","paper_title":"Appendix 2","paper_url":"https://democracy.caerphilly.gov.uk/documents/s56257/56257.pdf","headline":"\u00a32.047m (16.6% of total) savings have Red status and are not delivering in Q1","detail":"Of the council's \u00a312.3m planned savings, \u00a32.047m already has Red status in Q1. Most concerning: \u00a31.267m of these Red savings are within 'Transformation Savings Target' initiatives described as 'Commercially Sensitive', with no line-item breakdown. A further \u00a3618.5k is Amber (at risk), meaning 21.6% of the entire savings plan is off-track or at material risk.","category":"savings","matters":"A lender or finance director needs to know whether savings assumptions will hold. If \u00a32m of a \u00a312m plan is already slipping, the budget may not balance and may require in-year cuts or reserves.","figures":"Total savings \u00a312,331,837. Red \u00a32,047,000. Amber \u00a3618,564. Transformation targets: \u00a31,467,000 commercially sensitive item; \u00a32,000,000 management restructure","quote":"TOTAL 12,331,837    2,499,922     7,166,351     618,564        2,047,000","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-01"},"name":"Caerphilly","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-17","since_iso":"2026-08-18","distress":false,"headline":"Commercial estate income recovery is at risk; \u00a3100k of \u00a3200k saving is Amber","lead":"Council borrowing and financial standing often depends on property income. An income plan that is 50% uncertain in Q1 signals asset performance or market conditions are worse than budgeted.","also":["16 other findings in this window"],"watch":"Governance and Audit Committee on 2026-09-21","n_findings":17,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"Appendix 2","top_paper_url":"https://democracy.caerphilly.gov.uk/documents/s56257/56257.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":65,"news_drafts_total":3}}